  "ecological_interpretation": "Most of the apparent within-island concentration is compatible with neutral demographic attrition once shrinking island totals and absorbing local zeros are allowed to generate path dependence. Litchfield is the exception: its effective colony number collapsed substantially faster than this sequential neutral drift benchmark, indicating an additional local filter or disturbance beyond generic demographic thinning.",
  "paper_implication": "Reframe concentration as a two-component process: neutral attrition provides the background rule of colony-network erosion, whereas the Litchfield trajectory is a non-neutral collapse that motivates targeted habitat, snow, predation or disturbance tests. This is stronger than treating concentration itself as generic evidence for social facilitation."
